2026-01-31 21:38:41 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-31 21:38:41 | OUTPUT |     LOGICAL PUNCHLINE & TRUTH/RECOGNITION: Both are logical. Joke 2’s truth is more potent and universal—the driving force in many political defections is often careerist opportunism, not principle. The image of a politician thinking a potted plant is a better backdrop for re-election is a vivid, funny recognition of political vanity. Joke 1’s truth is about political grifters hopping between parties, which is also real, but the specific critique of Green recycling policies as "optimistic" is a milder, more policy-wonkish observation.
